## Testing

```bash
# Unit tests (no tape drive required)
go test ./internal/tape/... ./internal/ltfs/...

# All tests
go test ./...

# Integration test against a real / MHVTL tape device
TAPEFUSE_TEST_DEVICE=/dev/nst0 go test -v -run TestMHVTL ./internal/tape/...
```

The `TestMHVTL` test is automatically skipped when
`TAPEFUSE_TEST_DEVICE` is not set.

### MHVTL (virtual tape library)

[MHVTL](https://github.com/markh794/mhvtl) emulates a complete tape library
including robot and drives as real SCSI devices visible to the kernel.

```bash
# Install (Ubuntu/Debian)
sudo apt-get install mhvtl mt-st sg3-utils

# Load the kernel module
sudo modprobe mhvtl

# Start the virtual tape daemon
sudo vxd

# Confirm devices
ls /dev/st* /dev/nst*

# Run the integration test
TAPEFUSE_TEST_DEVICE=/dev/nst0 go test -v -run TestMHVTL ./internal/tape/...
```

